From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:56:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: PS4 GTT reclaim corrections (Orbis ge-0016)

NickLabs Orbis Graphics Engine 2.0.0-r3, audit findings GE-A01, GE-A02, GE-A09.

GE-A01 (reconciliation with the CVE-2026-52949 TTM fix):
- amdgpu_ttm_orbis_shrink_bo() no longer lets ttm_bo_shrink() move the buffer
  (allow_move=false). It first calls the new amdgpu_ttm_orbis_evict_to_system(),
  which validates to SYSTEM and then marks the move as an eviction
  (amdgpu_vm_bo_invalidate(bo, true)). A plain ttm_bo_validate() move notifies with
  evict=false, which leaves per-VM always-valid buffers only "moved": the next
  submission would update page tables to an unpopulated buffer.
- Backup failure handling relies on the backported TTM fixes (stable-6.15/0001,
  0002): the LRU walk advances past a buffer whose backup failed.

GE-A02 (active GTT trim):
- amdgpu_orbis_gtt_trim() walks the GTT LRU with the trylock cursor (two passes),
  skips buffers it cannot move (busy, no memory, not eviction-valuable) instead of
  stopping, is capped per call, and returns a full struct amdgpu_orbis_trim_result
  (requested, usage before/after, evicted, failed, skipped, first failure,
  interruption, cap, enforced). It returns 0 only when usage <= target.
- orbis_gtt_budget writes are serialised. The effective budget, the requested value,
  the state (enforced/over_budget/incomplete/interrupted) and the last trim are
  readable. A write whose trim did not bring usage under the budget returns -EBUSY
  (or -EINTR/-ERESTARTSYS); the new limit for allocations stays applied.

GE-A09 (GTT dmem cgroup region):
- The registration outcome is recorded and exposed in the read-only orbis_gtt_cgroup
  attribute: "registered region=gtt capacity=N" or "unavailable reason=param_off |
  no_cgroup_dmem | register_failed error=E | not_ps4".

Status: source-checked against 6.15.4 interfaces and checkpatch; not compiled here
(kernel compilation is done on the Nobara build machine).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CcGqiWDFgL3MdbGzpXfrDZ
