  *    (amdgpu_ttm_tt_populate -> ttm_tt_restore).
  *
  * Active trim: writing a lower orbis_gtt_budget evicts GTT buffers (LRU order) until usage is
- * within the budget, instead of waiting for the next allocation.
+ * within the budget, instead of waiting for the next allocation. ge-0016: the trim skips what
+ * it cannot move instead of stopping, never claims success it did not reach, and reports a
+ * full account (requested, usage before/after, evicted, failed, skipped, cap, interruption).
+ * Moves out of GTT are marked as evictions so per-VM buffers are revalidated before use.
  *
  * Off by default (amdgpu.orbis_shrinker=1 on the kernel command line enables it, PS4 only):
  * the backup capability must be set when a buffer's page table is created, so it cannot be
@@ -234,37 +237,77 @@ long amdgpu_orbis_shrinker_scan(struct amdgpu_device *adev, unsigned long nr_pag
 }
 
 /*
